## Key Architectural Principles

### 1. Contract-Based Design
Every macro must have explicit contracts:
```assembly
; @requires: stack aligned to 16 bytes
; @modifies: rax, rcx, rdi, rsi
; @returns: rax = result
; @throws: sets carry flag on error
macro risky_operation {
    ; implementation
}
```

### 2. Defensive Expansion
Macros should self-verify:
```assembly
macro check_alignment ptr*, alignment* {
    local .aligned, .done
    test ptr, (alignment* - 1)
    jz .aligned
    ; Handle misalignment
  .aligned:
}
```

### 3. Compositional Design
Each macro should be built from smaller, tested macros:
```assembly
macro safe_string_copy dest*, src*, max_len* {
    ; Built from strlen, memcpy, and bounds checking
}
```

